    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Self-hosted n8n only:** this version uses the community node `n8n-nodes-ashdocs` (n8n verification pending), so it runs on self-hosted n8n. The HTTP version of the same template uses only built-in nodes and also runs on n8n Cloud.\n\n\n## Generate monthly retainer invoices from Toggl Track time entries with ASHDOCS\n\nFreelancers and small agencies who track time in Toggl Track and bill clients monthly by the hour.\n\n### How it works\n1. On the 1st of each month at 08:00, **Get last month’s time entries** reads your Toggl Track time entries for the previous month (Toggl Track API v9, with client and project names).\n2. **Read rates** loads the **Rates** tab: one row per client and project with an hourly rate and the client’s billing email.\n3. **Build one invoice per client** adds up hours per client and project and turns them into line items (hours × rate).\n4. For each client, ASHDOCS finds or creates the customer, creates the invoice, and emails it.\n5. Every client ends up as a row in the **Invoice log** tab: sent with the invoice number, or skipped or failed with the reason (no rate, no email, API error).\n\n### Requirements\n- An ASHDOCS account (https://www.ashdocs.com/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template&utm_campaign=retainer-from-hours). Works on every ASHDOCS plan, including Free (100 credits a month).\n- A Toggl Track account\n- A Google Sheets account\n- Self-hosted n8n with the community node `n8n-nodes-ashdocs` installed\n\n[ASHDOCS](https://www.ashdocs.com/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template&utm_campaign=retainer-from-hours) · [Docs](https://www.ashdocs.com/docs)",
        "height": 740,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "e24291b2-70be-45dd-a6b7-b5e490b0ccae",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1160,
        -320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup\n**Plan:** Works on every ASHDOCS plan, including Free (100 credits a month).\n\n1. Create an ASHDOCS account at https://www.ashdocs.com/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template&utm_campaign=retainer-from-hours and create an API key on the **API Keys** page of the dashboard. A test key makes watermarked test invoices while you try the workflow.\n2. Install the ASHDOCS community node: **Settings → Community nodes → Install**, enter `n8n-nodes-ashdocs`. Then open any ASHDOCS node and create the **ASHDOCS API** credential with your key.\n3. Toggl Track: copy your API token from **Profile settings** and create a **Basic Auth** credential named **Toggl Track API token**: User = the token, Password = `api_token`.\n4. Create a Google Sheet with two tabs. **Rates**: Client, Project, Hourly Rate, Billing Email (leave Project empty for a client-wide rate). **Invoice log**: Month, Client, Status, Invoice Number, Hours, Total, Pay Link. Pick them in **Read rates**, **Log invoice** and **Log problem**.\n5. Fill in **Settings**: currency, payment terms, and whether to bill only billable time.\n6. Run **Test workflow** once. Clients without a rate or email are logged as skipped, not invoiced.",
        "height": 500,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "7c7085fa-bdb9-4edd-a2a7-b5d5644c7ef8",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -580,
        -320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Customize\n- This reads the time entries of the Toggl user whose token you use. For a team, call Toggl’s Reports API for the workspace in **Get last month’s time entries** instead.\n- Round hours differently, or add a minimum monthly fee, in **Build one invoice per client**.\n- Create drafts for review instead of sending: remove **Send invoice** and set Issue off in **Create invoice**.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "d7bf14ae-6022-48ec-acfe-c367d959594f",
      "name": "Customize",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -580,
        220
      ]
    }
